   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Truco: cơm y gạo",
    "@en": "Trick: cơm and gạo"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**gạo** es el arroz crudo (el que compras) y **cơm** el arroz cocido (el que comes). **ăn cơm** (literalmente «comer arroz») significa simplemente «comer».",
     "@en": "**gạo** is raw rice (the one you buy) and **cơm** is cooked rice (the one you eat). **ăn cơm** (literally «eat rice») means simply «eat»."
    },
    {
     "@es": "La carne se dice **thịt** + animal: **thịt gà** (pollo), **thịt bò** (ternera), **thịt heo** (cerdo; en el norte, **thịt lợn**).",
     "@en": "The meat is called **thịt** + animal: **thịt gà** (chicken), **thịt bò** (veal), **thịt heo** (pig; in the north, **thịt lợn**)."
    }
   ]
  },
